  "explanation": {
    "sms": "SoilSense plan: 2027 Fallow (no crop); 2028 Winter wheat; 2029 Grain sorghum. Based on NASA climate data 1991-2025. Check with your extension agent.",
    "speech": "NASA data for your field near Finney County, KS shows growing degree days rising by about 68 degree days per decade, and that change is statistically real. Focusing on a balance of profit, soil and risk, I suggest fallow in 2027, then winter wheat in 2028, then grain sorghum in 2029. Please check with your county extension agent before buying seed.",
    "summary": "NASA data for your field near Finney County, KS shows growing degree days (May–Sep) rising by about 68 °F·days per decade, and that change is statistically real. Recommended for a balance of profit, soil and risk: Fallow (no crop) → Winter wheat → Grain sorghum. Compared with continuing the current pattern (Soybean → Corn → Soybean): estimated −$54/acre per year, 66 lb/acre more nitrogen over 3 years, and a soil-health score of 36 vs 48 out of 100.",
  },
